{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1196250-help-with-the-turn-system","id":1196250,"title":"Help with the turn system","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-03-16T15:41:14-07:00","id":1196250,"title":"Help with the turn system","content":"I've been playing the cWoD (and sometimes COfD), so I'm familiar with the storyteller system. I'm &quot;studying&quot; scion, and I've understood pretty much everything except for the turn system, which (I might be obtuse) I'm struggling with<br /> <br /> Any quick explanation?<br /> Sorry for bothering<br /> <br /> <br /> Edit: I'm using the first edition, if that matters","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My English sucks. Sorry.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23549-toreadorgentleman","name":"ToreadorGentleman","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-17T00:19:50-07:00","id":1196398,"title":"","content":"First Edition. Yeah, that DOES help, but... Okay, everyone rolls Wits + Awareness, if memory serves. This assigns order. Keep your Epic Wits in mind.<br /> <br /> You start with the one who got the most successes, they take their action, and then they need to wait a number of 'ticks' equal to the speed of their action before acting again. Most standard actions have a speed of 5, some swifter weapons have a speed of 4, for example.<br /> <br /> Repeat until everyone's dead.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-17T07:20:54-07:00","id":1196468,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1196250-help-with-the-turn-system?p=1196398#post1196398\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">First Edition. Yeah, that DOES help, but... Okay, everyone rolls Wits + Awareness, if memory serves. This assigns order. Keep your Epic Wits in mind.<br /> <br /> You start with the one who got the most successes, they take their action, and then they need to wait a number of 'ticks' equal to the speed of their action before acting again. Most standard actions have a speed of 5, some swifter weapons have a speed of 4, for example.<br /> <br /> Repeat until everyone's dead.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Thanks you so so much!<br /> That was really helpful","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My English sucks. Sorry.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23549-toreadorgentleman","name":"ToreadorGentleman","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}